     "question": "Does the baseline reproduction's success probability at the headline configuration match the paper's reported ~0.2?",
     "reason": "Reproduced success probability is far from 0.2, indicating a misconfigured baseline.",
     "judge_reason": "The headline native baseline succeeds with probability 0.4946524, and the common-polar baseline with 0.4974534. Both lie outside the stipulated approximately 0.14–0.26 interval around 0.2. The separate source audit's 0.2157546 occurs at a different configuration and does not satisfy this headline condition.",
     "evidence": [
      "proposal/logs/direct_controls/beta_nk6_K20.75_beta0.745_e0.001_nx6_t0.0125/result.json",
      "proposal/logs/polar_runs/beta_nk6_K20.75_beta0.745_e0.001_nx6_t0.0125/result.json",
