     "rubric": "direction",
     "gate": "G3",
     "code": "criterion_not_met",
     "observed_value": "boundaries_partial",
     "accepted_values": [
      "boundaries_clear"
     ],
     "question": "Does the characterization identify the regime boundaries (crossover points where a different family wins) between baseline and variant?",
     "reason": "Paper notes regime differences but does not identify the boundaries precisely.",
     "judge_reason": "The report identifies concrete feasibility differences: beta misses the (5,0.01) and (6,0.003) targets while both families pass (7,0.001). It also documents direct-versus-QSVT implementation crossovers. However, the three common-QSVT characterization points all favor f2, and a kernel-family winner boundary in the (n_k,epsilon) plane is not localized; the reported implementation crossovers also change time or compiler.",
     "evidence": [
      "proposal/sections/results.tex:88–120",
      "proposal/sections/discussion.tex:43–58",
      "proposal/figures/resolution.pdf",
      "proposal/figures/implementation_crossover.pdf"
